data an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_int_argument_inhabits_a_nat_parameter_at_typecheck" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the seed accepts an Int-typed argument at a Nat parameter. Int = GroupCompletion<Nat> strictly contains Nat, so Int to Nat is partial; the implicit route is not total, and gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate (coercion is the implicit-safe subset) refuses it. It is admitted ONLY through a declared checked conversion returning Optional (ruling `where_refinements_retire_for_checked_constructors`) or carried evidence, or as an in-range literal introduced at the expected type. Nat to Int, and UInt to Nat (alias), remain admitted.",

    "HARM: a negative Int reaches a Nat consumer; observed as a runtime divergence (call depth 100000) while a non-negative one passes silently, so the wrongness is invisible until a negative occurs. RUNG FOUND AT: silent until a runtime negative (below the ladder). ATTAINABLE CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the front-end inhabitance judgment refuses Int at a Nat position unless a declared route is named; the capability restored is expected-type-directed literal introduction replacing the types-only numeric arm.",

    "ROUTE, BY READING (unrun): `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance` reaches its `declared_realizes_as_kernel_numeric` arm, which asks only the produced numeral type and `v1.compiler.coercion` `provenance_realizes_natively` of the declared provenance. That predicate is types-only, so it cannot tell an Int VALUE from a numeral LITERAL. Repair: replace the numeric arm with literal introduction at the expected type.",

    "EVIDENCE: witness `dag/test/claim/int_argument_at_nat_parameter_witness.dag` (branch int-at-nat-red), UNRUN: RED Int parameter at Nat; controls Nat value, non-negative literal, Nat to Int widening; the negative-literal RED status is unknown until run. Raw outputs and fixtures: zesty-badger-599 ~/zb-evidence, seed sha256 747ed06b.. (f20cdcc799ee), tree 761485283f2f, fixtures 08bfd3da.. and ce388ada.., outputs 9ef686fa.. and 202791d1... The v2 probe there was assembly-rejected including its control: INVALID, no v2 verdict.",

    "7-KIND RED (zesty-badger-599, srv1 ~/zb-evidence/k7.log sha256 741b255780039b4db5266c0d0a6be20705183f4646df2e68bc63733c414ab933; fixtures zz_k_<kind>.dag, tree 761485283f2, seed 747ed06b from f20cdcc799ee): the record and generic-T arms stand as siblings of Int-at-Nat; the coproduct arm is WITHDRAWN (NonNegative at the std.integer Int parameter accepted, and the fixture cannot tell std.integer.Int from the kernel Int).","SIBLING, CITED NOT DUPLICATED: the `std.integer` UInt8 = Compose<UInt, MachineWidth<8>> phantom hole (transparent to Int; base64_octets [256,0,0]). Also M2c and #15441. The recursion symptom stays with clever T9.",

    "STATED OUT, OWNED BY Q4: a Char value at a declared Int (a branded Int alias) is a distinct case not claimed closed by the numeric-arm repair. Candidate admitting arms, by reading and unrun: (a) `alias_identity_in_judgment`, (b) the terminal `Inhabits` fall-through of `declared_type_inhabitance`. A probe separating them is unrun.",
    "SHARP-STAG-549 RAN RELATED STRING-FAMILY PROBES 2026-11-19, REVISED 2026-11-23 (NOT the Char-value-at-declared-Int case this row's STATED OUT line owes, which stays OWED and unrun; scratch module probe.alias_interchange, harness gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census on the v1 seed CompileAccept path, one gunbc run --claim-run process, seed binary built release from this checkout): a String-typed VARIABLE at a std.types NonEmptyStr parameter (where string_non_empty), at a branded std.types PathSegment (NonEmptyStr where brand(...)), at a local bare nickname type MyStr = String, and at a local type MySecret nominal_opaque = String EACH produce ZERO blocking rows of any class -- fully and silently admitted -- while an Int at a declared record parameter, a String variable at a declared record parameter, and an Int at a declared String parameter are each refused (blocking), and base-at-base and derived-at-derived controls are clean. This SEPARATES THE ARMS this row left open, for the String family: the admitting path is the alias/refinement transparency inside `declared_type_inhabitance` (v1.compiler.infer_types `alias_identity_in_judgment` returns true for a bare alias, which its caller v1.compiler.infer `declared_type_inhabitance` turns into Inhabits; `refinement_inhabitance` returns Undecidable (UndecidableRefinementIntroduction), which the application does not treat as blocking), NOT the numeric arm. It is therefore a DISTINCT family from this row's Int-subsumes-Nat numeric arm and is NOT closed by the numeric-arm repair. Under gunbc.design_ruling::type_relationships_are_declared_and_transparent_reference_is_explicit_2026_11_23 the admission of a base String argument, without the required construction or evidence, at a RESTRICTED (NonEmptyStr), a BRANDED (PathSegment), or an explicitly-nominal (`nominal_opaque = String`) parameter is a RED the plan gunbc.plans.derived_types_keep_their_name must REACH (a nominal distinction is not erased because its representation matches the base); the bare `type MyStr = String` admission is recorded as an OBSERVATION only -- the equals form is not selected as transparent-reference syntax and its classification is an open surface question -- so it is not counted as a defect here. The Char-value-at-declared-Int experiment (a branded Int alias) is a separate, still-unrun probe these String-family runs do not close. The v2 REAL-PATH String-at-NonEmptyStr verdict is STILL OWED (this probe ran the v1 seed path; the v2 claim remains citable only over two-declaration stand-ins).",

    "INTERPRETATION CLARIFIED 2026-11-23, NOT A NEW EXECUTION RECEIPT: gunbc.design_ruling::type_relationships_are_declared_and_transparent_reference_is_explicit_2026_11_23 and gunbc.design_argument::declared_intent distinguish transparent same-identity reference from constraint or nominal erasure. The historical four accepted inputs above remain the observed v1 results; acceptance of type MyStr = String is not by itself a defect or a required refusal. An explicitly transparent reference to the same full type belongs among the positive controls, including when that type is a constrained composition. Its spelling is still a language-design choice: the existing equals form is not canonized by its current behavior, and the operator's value-copy reading states an expectation rather than a runtime copying rule. The plan keeps the real v2 verdict owed and the constrained/nominal cases as separate obligations; no generic-form exemption or blanket alias ban is inferred.",

    "OPEN ITEM, NOT DONE: the REAL-PATH v2 claim is OWED. `v2.test.claim.compiler.infer_int_argument_at_nat_parameter_witness` runs over two-declaration stand-ins for std.nat Nat and std.integer Int and is citable only as v2's structural judgment refusing a distinct product at a distinct product, never as v2 refusing Int at std.nat Nat. TRIGGER: an ingest that resolves the real std.nat Nat and std.integer Int with their kernel grounding.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
